  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "After creating a binary resource in Fedora 6 through the web interface, I can use SPARQL-Update to add and delete a second ebucore:hasMimeType property to it, but I cannot modify or remove the initial default application/octet-stream value.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
        "text": "@Ben Pennell"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " confirmed this problem, noting that it is not occurring in Fedora 5 but is occurring in Fedora 6. He said: \"My recollection is that ebucore:hasMimeType is generated from the header file for the binary, and the value from the header file is used for the HEAD/GET responses for the binary. But updating the RDF description for the binary has no impact on the binary's content type header.\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
