  "description": "<p>After creating a binary resource in Fedora 6 through the web interface, I can use SPARQL-Update to add and delete a second ebucore:hasMimeType property to it, but I cannot modify or remove the initial default application/octet-stream value.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6\" data-account-id=\"5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6\" accountid=\"5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Ben Pennell</a> confirmed this problem, noting that it is not occurring in Fedora 5 but is occurring in Fedora 6. He said: \"My recollection is that ebucore:hasMimeType is generated from the header file for the binary, and the value from the header file is used for the HEAD/GET responses for the binary. But updating the RDF description for the binary has no impact on the binary's content type header.\"</p>",
